      "created_at": "2012-05-03T22:17:46.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Christopher&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Christopher\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"awp832\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> awp832:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Here I am trying to be cagey and you guys have to go and outfox me.    Ok,  fine,  lets just <span class=\"bbcode-i\">suppose</span> for the sake of argument that there were say,   nine villan character cards.   How would it work then?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’ll go ahead and back this up. The Ennead deck does in fact feature 9 villain character cards.  They all have the villain type.</p>\n<p>And it works much more seamlessly than I anticipated when I originally drafted the concept.  I was honestly afraid it would be a massive mess.  But so far, so good!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Oh man, hearing stuff like that just makes me want to playtest even more… the 17th needs to get here ASAP! And so does the $75k mark. ;D</p>",
